# SAB Product Definition (mandatory)

Before adding or changing product functionality, read and follow:

`docs/Smart_App_Builder_Revamp_Product_Definition.md`

That file is the complete technical/product document for this project (brief, PRD, personas, journeys, functional spec, IA).

## How to use it

- Treat it as the source of truth for scope, flows, objects/fields/layouts, create/edit/deploy behavior, and UX principles.
- Do not invent features that conflict with it. If a request conflicts, follow the document and call out the gap.
- Reuse existing SAB capabilities; do not discard enterprise behavior for a simpler demo.
- Prefer **application-first**, **progressive disclosure**, **visual feedback** (graph/preview updates in real time), and **contextual configuration**.
- Keep advanced settings available but secondary (do not dump all 13+ sections into the primary path).
- Distinguish **existing SAB behavior** from items the document labels as **recommendations**.

## Current prototype focus

This workspace currently prototypes the Objects graph and object create/edit flow. When extending it, align with the document’s object modeling, field types, relationships, live visual feedback, and deploy-to-inspect behavior.
